    {
      "id": 142,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        93.07523017014603,
        4525.51911695022
      ],
      "size": [
        330,
        330
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 13,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "Note: Project Suite",
      "properties": {
        "ue_properties": {
          "widget_ue_connectable": {},
          "version": "7.6",
          "input_ue_unconnectable": {}
        }
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## H3 Project Suite\n\n**The loop:** Queue \u2192 open the panel \u2192 watch \u2192 Approve \u2192 change the prompt \u2192 Queue again.\n\n1. Name your project on the **Hub** node.\n2. Queue. Clip 1 renders normally \u2014 nothing to bypass.\n3. Click **Open project\u2026** on the Hub, watch it, hit **Approve**.\n4. Change the prompt and queue again. Clip 2 continues clip 1.\n\nQueue *without* approving and you get another take of the same clip, so you can iterate on a prompt freely.\n\n**Context length** is how much of the previous clip carries over: 22 is a good default, 39\u201356 for slow scenes.\n\n**SaveVideo** still writes to output/video as normal. The project keeps its own copy, so you can mute SaveVideo if you only want the project's files.\n\nFirst frame only matters for clip 1; later clips continue from the chain, not from the image."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
